# Content changes

English, first person, plain. No emoji in titles. Do not invent credits, lyrics, dates, or ratings. Look them up. Do not commit unless asked.

## Media lists

Edit `_data/books.yml`, `music.yml`, `movies.yml`, or `games.yml`. Put the entry in the matching `years` group (`label: YYYY`), **newest date first**. Use `current:` only for in-progress books/games.

Shared fields: `title`, Wikipedia `url` when it exists, `date` (YYYY-MM-DD, the day Stefano finished/listened/watched/played), `rating` (1–5), `year` (work year), `genres` (lowercase; quote keys like `"R&B"`).

- Books: `authors: [{name, url}]`, `language`
- Music: `artists: [{name, url}]`
- Movies: `creators: [{name, url}]` (director), `language`
- Games: `developers`, `publishers`, `console: {name, url}`

Copy the surrounding YAML shape. Do not invent people or links.

## Posts

`_posts/YYYY-MM-DD-slug.markdown`. Filename date = front-matter date.

```yaml
layout: post
title:  "Title without emoji"
date:   YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS +0100
icon: name          # required if the post is not tied to a project
categories: one-or-more
```

- Project write-up: `categories` must include that project's `category` (see `_data/projects.yml`). The project icon then wins via `post-label.html`.
- Standalone post: set `icon:` (e.g. `music`, `website`).
- Voice matches `_posts/2026-08-16-rebuilding-this-site.markdown` and `_posts/2026-07-03-magia-bianca.markdown`.
- Cursor-authored posts end with `{% include made-with-cursor.html %}` (`— Made with [icon-cursor] Cursor`, muted, right-aligned). `icon-cursor` is the hexagon + arrow cutout, not a mouse pointer.

### Album / listen post (see Magia Bianca)

Order: personal opener → cover (`assets/images/posts/`, `.album-cover`) → Stefano's favorites → `<aside class="album-facts">` with label `Album information` (facts only, smaller muted text) → `.listen-links` (Spotify, YouTube Music, Apple Music) → made-with.

Date = the `date` already in `music.yml` for that album. Quote published lyrics only. Verify streaming URLs; do not invent YouTube Music album IDs.

## Projects

Add a block to `_data/projects.yml`. If `section` is new, also add the `assign` + `##` heading in `projects.markdown`.

Required: `slug`, `section` (`flagship` | `libraries` | `web` | `games` | `interpreters`), `category` (must match related posts), `icon`, `name`, `why` (one line), `description` (`>` markdown), `links`, `tags`. Optional: `screenshot`, `screenshot_alt`, `emoji`.

Related posts are automatic when `post.categories` contains `project.category`.

## Icons

New mark: `<symbol id="icon-NAME" viewBox="0 0 24 24">` in `_includes/icons.svg`. Prefer the site stroke style (`currentColor`, width 1.75). Use `{% include icon.html name="NAME" %}`.

Give it an unused color in `assets/main.scss` next to the other `.icon.icon-*` rules.

Taken: mappa `#2dd4bf`, todo `#f4b942`, prettycode `#a78bfa`, blocchi `#60a5fa`, fifteen `#fb923c`, tictactoe `#fb7185`, connectfour `#facc15`, turing `#ef4444`, brainfuck `#e879f9`, website `#f43f5e`, music-in-posts `#f472b6`, spotify `#1ed760`, youtube-music `#ff0033`, apple-music `#fc3c44`.

- Project / global: `.icon.icon-NAME { color: #...; }`
- Post-only (keep nav brand): `.post-title .icon.icon-NAME, .post-link .icon.icon-NAME`
- Music and website post icons: not green or blue
